Package: ristools
Title: Faithful Reading and Writing of RIS and BibTeX Bibliographic Files
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Mark", "Engelbert", email = "mengelbert@3ieimpact.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads and writes RIS, BibTeX, Medline and Web of Science
    bibliographic files without the data loss that affects several existing
    implementations. Multiple values in a single field (authors, keywords, JEL
    descriptors, ISSNs) are joined with a delimiter that cannot occur in
    bibliographic text, so the record-to-data-frame conversion is lossless and
    reversible. Also preserves page-range order, trailing punctuation in
    titles, and tags containing digits. Depends only on base R.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    stats
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
